pet Archon helped me afford the exorbitant rates of shopkeeper.  Nice thing
about Archons, they often kill shopkeepers quickly enough for one to collect
their healing potions.

One of the first "Major Steps" toward surviving pacifism is buying 2
much-needed level-ups from the Oracle, so once that dlvl was reached, care
was taken to keep the pet Archon away from the Oracle until the buying of
first a major Oracle counsel, then a minor Oracle counsel (in that order).
I always try and avoid it, but forget to keep powerful pets away from the
Oracle, then there's only one thing you can do: make a tin of Oracle meat.

Grabbing the 1st Sokoban level's loot and food, w592 then made a quick trip
to minetown, getting [ofDex, a boH, luckstone and stethoscope from small
bones piles.  Woo-hoo.  Gnomish Mines below Minetown and Soko above level 1
remained unexplored in the game.

Later on dlvl 8 or 9 a shop yielded a /poly and w592 collected spellbooks
and got many spells, including the ultimate pacifist spell: charm monster,
and ID, too.  This shop also had a bullwhip, and the Archon's Demonbane was
replaced by the +7 Excalibur from a bones level and ?EW picked up along the
way.  Do yourself a favor - give your Archon an Excalibur.  (S)he makes quic
k work of everything, except high-level Rodneys, but that was later (see
number of kills - Rodney increases his level by one with each appearance).

Thus equipped, the Archon cleared a path down to and through the Castle
level, and allowed w592 to remain low level, quaffing b!EH (which were
smoky) for the extra HP, snagging the castle WoW.

After reaching VoD (a bones level there had another WoW(0:0), but this was
eaten quickly by a pet Xorn) and sorting through all the loot, w592 mapped
much of Gehennom.  Asmodeus and Baalzebub never asked for bribes, just
attacked at first meeting.  Since they're higher level than the average
Archon, black dragons' breath was a good way to deal with these big demons.
W592 found the vibrating square, got Vlad's candle holder then wanted the
bell of Opening and so needed to raise her alignment to do the quest.

She headed back to some kitchen sinks in the upper levels to do some
Foocubi-consorting, one of the only ways to raise alignment as an chaotic
atheist pacifist.  Mental note: don't let the pet kill the Foocubus!  After
alignment was raise sufficiently and several c?Geno of wraiths to level-up
to xlvl 14, the quest proved no great challenge, and it was Rodney's turn.


The pet Archon was around level 35 from some !GL so the first few encounters
with the wiz of Yendor were trivial.  After the wiz's level exceeded the
Archon's, I reverse geno'ed black dragons as the method of dealing with
Rodney's pesky re-appearences.




